{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/615974-totem-communication-questions","id":615974,"title":"Totem communication questions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-04T21:42:19-07:00","id":615974,"title":"Totem communication questions.","content":"I don't have the book with me, so I cannot look, but me, and a bunch of friends where trying to figure out, and arguing,about it, how the Uratha communicate with their Totem. I mean, imagine a pack of 5 werewolves of average experiences, and a typical Totem of average power. Some said it was only under specific circumstances, other said that it was like some sort of permanent telepathy, like a link, and others told me that it was up to the storyteller, cause there was no definitive answer in book.<br /> <br /> Since I don't have the book with me, I can't look. Will get my book back only in 4 days.<br /> <br /> In any case, what is the official answer to this... or if there are none, what is YOUR personal answer ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:05:33-07:00","id":616000,"title":"","content":"The Uratha can either speak or hear across the gauntlet. Members of the pack are always resonant with their totem, so a totem can use that as a jumping board to reach across after some doing, staying in Twilight where the Uratha can speak to them or actually manifesting to talk to them. Or the Uratha could step across and just talk to them in the Hisil. There's also a few rites that make the totem manifest.<br /> <br /> The totem might have a numen that would act as a sort of telepathy. Just looking there's Implant Mission, which causes obsession regarding carrying the mission out and might upset werewolves, but there's also Sign, which allows the totem to send messages 'in any media.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:05:42-07:00","id":616002,"title":"","content":"You'd need a manifestation or a numina for permanent telepathic communication, or Pack Awareness gift. Aside from that, the totem needs to be relatively close to it's pack in order to confer it's blessings, something like within a mile or two, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:20:17-07:00","id":616005,"title":"","content":"Something to keep in mind is that the totem is a full pack member, just like any of the player character Uratha or wolf blooded or humans who are also a part of the pack. They exist in the Shadow by default, so if you're near them, and in the shadow....they can talk to you. So long as you understand First Tongue, no problem! It sounds like your players may be under the impression of, is that the totem is some sort of distant patron bestowing it's blessings from on high, which is very much not the case. Totems are immediate, you talk to them, you MIGHT even be friendly with them, and they in particular can help you hunt in the shadow, and sometimes in the flesh in the methods mentioned above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}